# No trailing slash, so this covers a symlinked `node_modules` as well as a real
# one. This checkout lives in iCloud Drive, which evicts the contents of files it
# thinks are cold — leaving entries that report their true size and read back as
# zero bytes, so eslint and Next fail with errors that look like version
# conflicts (`Ajv__default.default is not a constructor`) rather than like
# missing data. Pointing `node_modules` at a `.nosync` directory does not survive
# npm: both `npm ci` and `npm install` delete the path and recreate it as a real
# directory, so the symlink silently disappears on the next install.
node_modules
node_modules.nosync/
.next/
out/
build/
.DS_Store
*.pem
.env*
!.env.example
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.next-dev.log
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Supabase CLI link state — machine-local, contains no secrets but no value in git
supabase/.temp/

# Worktrees created by the harness. Git-ignored scratch: the branch inside
# carries the work, and an unignored worktree directory is how an entire
# second checkout gets committed into the repository by a stray `git add -A`.
.claude/worktrees/

# Claude Code personal settings (permissions, local overrides)
.claude/settings.local.json

# iCloud conflict copies. This checkout lives in iCloud Drive (see the
# node_modules note above), and when the sync client sees a batch of files
# appear — a merge, a branch switch — it can duplicate them as `name 2.ext`
# alongside the originals. Sixty-nine of them appeared during one merge.
#
# Ignored for the same reason `.claude/worktrees/` is: a stray `git add -A`
# is all it takes to commit an entire second copy of the source tree. The
# companion entries in eslint.config.mjs and tsconfig.json matter as much,
# because neither tool reads this file — without them the copies stay
# invisible to git while still being linted and typechecked.
#
# Deliberately `[2-9]` rather than `[0-9]`: a file legitimately named
# `figure 1.png` is plausible in a docs directory, and a tenth conflict copy
# is not. Nothing tracked in this repository matches the pattern.
* [2-9].*
* [2-9]/
